.IX Title "YaraFFI::Event 3pm"
.TH YaraFFI::Event 3pm 2025-10-30 "perl v5.38.2" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
YaraFFI::Event \- Event class that stringifies to rule name but also works as a hash
.SH VERSION
.IX Header "VERSION"
Version 0.07
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    use YaraFFI::Event;
\&
\&    # Create a rule match event with metadata
\&    my $event = YaraFFI::Event\->new(
\&        event    => \*(Aqrule_match\*(Aq,
\&        rule     => \*(AqMalwareRule\*(Aq,
\&        metadata => {
\&            author      => \*(AqSecurity Team\*(Aq,
\&            description => \*(AqDetects malware\*(Aq,
\&            severity    => 5,
\&            active      => 1,
\&        },
\&    );
\&
\&    print "Matched: $event\en";  # Stringifies to rule name
\&    print "Author: ", $event\->metadata\->{author}, "\en";
\&    print "Severity: ", $event\->severity, "\en";
\&
\&    # Create a string match event with offsets
\&    my $str_event = YaraFFI::Event\->new(
\&        event     => \*(Aqstring_match\*(Aq,
\&        rule      => \*(AqMalwareRule\*(Aq,
\&        string_id => \*(Aq$suspicious\*(Aq,
\&        offsets   => [0, 42, 128],
\&    );
\&
\&    print "String: ", $str_event\->string_id, "\en";
\&    print "Found at: ", join(", ", @{$str_event\->offsets}), "\en";
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\f(CW\*(C`YaraFFI::Event\*(C'\fR represents a scanning event from \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR. It can be used as a string
(stringifies to the rule name) or as a hash/object to access event details.
.PP
Events are created during \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR scans and passed to callback functions.
.SH "EVENT TYPES"
.IX Header "EVENT TYPES"
.SS rule_match
.IX Subsection "rule_match"
Emitted when a \f(CW\*(C`YARA\*(C'\fR rule matches the scanned data.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    Fields:
\&        event    => \*(Aqrule_match\*(Aq
\&        rule     => \*(AqRuleName\*(Aq
\&        metadata => { key => value, ... }  # Optional, rule metadata
.Ve
.SS string_match
.IX Subsection "string_match"
Emitted when a string pattern within a rule matches.
.PP
.Vb 5
\&    Fields:
\&        event     => \*(Aqstring_match\*(Aq
\&        rule      => \*(AqRuleName\*(Aq
\&        string_id => \*(Aq$string_identifier\*(Aq
\&        offsets   => [offset1, offset2, ...]  # Byte offsets where string matched
.Ve
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS new(%args)
.IX Subsection "new(%args)"
Creates a new event object.
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    my $event = YaraFFI::Event\->new(
\&        event => \*(Aqrule_match\*(Aq,
\&        rule  => \*(AqTestRule\*(Aq,
\&    );
.Ve
.SS event
.IX Subsection "event"
Returns the event type (\f(CW\*(C`rule_match\*(C'\fR or \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $type = $event\->event;
.Ve
.SS rule
.IX Subsection "rule"
Returns the name of the matched rule.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $rule_name = $event\->rule;
.Ve
.SS metadata
.IX Subsection "metadata"
Returns the rule metadata as a hash reference (\f(CW\*(C`rule_match\*(C'\fR events only).
.PP
.Vb 5
\&    my $meta = $event\->metadata;
\&    if ($meta) {
\&        print "Author: $meta\->{author}\en";
\&        print "Severity: $meta\->{severity}\en";
\&    }
.Ve
.SS string_id
.IX Subsection "string_id"
Returns the string identifier (\f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR events only).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $id = $event\->string_id;  # e.g., \*(Aq$suspicious\*(Aq
.Ve
.SS offsets
.IX Subsection "offsets"
Returns an array reference of byte offsets where the string matched (\f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR events only).
.PP
.Vb 4
\&    my $offsets = $event\->offsets;
\&    for my $offset (@$offsets) {
\&        print "Match at byte $offset\en";
\&    }
.Ve
.SS "Convenience Metadata Accessors"
.IX Subsection "Convenience Metadata Accessors"
For common metadata fields, you can access them directly:
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    my $author = $event\->author;
\&    my $desc   = $event\->description;
\&    my $sev    = $event\->severity;
.Ve
.PP
These return undef if the metadata doesn't exist or the field isn't present.
.SS has_metadata
.IX Subsection "has_metadata"
Returns true if the event has metadata.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    if ($event\->has_metadata) {
\&        # Process metadata
\&    }
.Ve
.SS has_offsets
.IX Subsection "has_offsets"
Returns true if the event has match offsets.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    if ($event\->has_offsets) {
\&        print "Matches at: ", join(", ", @{$event\->offsets}), "\en";
\&    }
.Ve
.SS match_count
.IX Subsection "match_count"
Returns the number of times the string matched (for \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR events).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $count = $event\->match_count;
.Ve
.SS is_rule_match
.IX Subsection "is_rule_match"
Returns true if this is a rule_match event.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    if ($event\->is_rule_match) {
\&        # Handle rule match
\&    }
.Ve
.SS is_string_match
.IX Subsection "is_string_match"
Returns true if this is a \f(CW\*(C`string_match\*(C'\fR event.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    if ($event\->is_string_match) {
\&        # Handle string match
\&    }
.Ve
.SS to_hash
.IX Subsection "to_hash"
Returns the event as a plain hash reference.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $hash = $event\->to_hash;
.Ve
.SH OVERLOADING
.IX Header "OVERLOADING"
The event object overloads string concatenation, so it can be used directly
in print statements and will display the rule name:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    print "Matched: $event\en";  # Prints "Matched: RuleName"
.Ve
